/**
 * SemanticSurface skin (DS-A004).
 *
 * Public terminology is “semantic surface roles”. The historic
 * `--ds-material-*` prefix is retained only as a compatibility channel between
 * the BrandTheme/Appearance compilers and this skin; it does not refer to
 * Material UI or any external component framework.
 *
 * Every role maps governed channels into private local variables. One shared
 * state machine then paints the component, preventing role blocks from
 * drifting and keeping nested surfaces isolated.
 *
 * Phase B (second premium pass) additions — the role projections above are
 * untouched; everything below the state machine is additive:
 *
 *   - Material layer map: base fill (1) and bounded tint/texture (2) come from
 *     the role background/texture channels; the optical edge (3) is the
 *     `::before` highlight; state washes (4) are the hover/active/selected
 *     channel swaps; the focus ring (5) is the independent `::after`. No
 *     decoration is painted unless a channel authors it, so
 *     `effectIntensity: 0` tenants keep full canvas → panel → raised
