 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as the other engine skins (P-47):
 * every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity. Unlayered outranks
 * preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the panel's outer `<div>`, which carries the pair
 * `ds-pattern-detail-panel ds-engine-modern` + `data-part='root'` +
 * `data-pattern='detail-panel'`; every painted element is a descendant with
 * its own `data-part`. The engine has two roots -- the content panel and the
 * loading early-return -- and both carry all three stamps.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48 + 4th-wave recount): the Platform-only Rottay artifact
 * ships an unlayered `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at
 * (0,3,1) that sets `border-color` on every element. Every border-painting
 * rule here reaches (0,4,0) WITHOUT repeating an attribute: the two scope
 * classes lend (0,2,0) and the remaining (0,2,0) comes from the panel root's
 * own always-present `[data-part='root']` (descendants) or the root's own
 * `[data-pattern='detail-panel']` stamp (the root rule itself). FRAGILITY
 * NOTE: if a future render drops either stamp, restore the stamp rather than
 * re-doubling a part. The border-specificity lint in
 * `PatternDetailPanel.real-engines.test.tsx` enforces the floor.
 *
 * COMPOSITION (pattern law): action buttons, the back button and the loading
 * skeleton are the certified Button/Skeleton primitives -- their paint,
 * hover/press/focus, forced-colors and touch floors live in those primitives'
 * own skins. The rules below paint ONLY pattern-owned chrome: the panel
 * surface, the header identity frame, the pattern's tab anatomy (pinned by
 * the quality contract -- composing the Tabs primitive is a tests-side
 * contract change, recorded as debt), breadcrumbs, and the danger action
 * variant the Button contract does not offer (quiet destructive secondary).
 *
 * Interaction paint that the removed React hover/focus state used to own now
 * lives here as `:hover` (hover-capable only, 4th-wave law), `:focus`
 * (pointer-agnostic) and `:active` (the touch equivalent), gated on
 * `:not(:disabled)` because the button element is natively `disabled`
 * whenever the action is disabled OR loading -- the exact `isInteractive`
 * gate the JSX evaluated.
 *
 * Values are transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx` (inline styles
 * drained: tab geometry, breadcrumbs, headings, header/footer layout and the
 * body/sidebar flex contract -- the last inline layout is the sidebar's
 * runtime width channel).
 */

/* ---- root: card surface + radius (was containerStyle) ---- */
.ds-pattern-detail-panel.ds-engine-modern[data-part='root'] {
  --ds-detail-panel-padding: clamp(var(--ds-spacing-4, 16px), 2vw, var(--ds-spacing-6, 24px));
  --ds-detail-panel-section-gap: var(--ds-spacing-5, 20px);
  --ds-detail-panel-content-gap: var(--ds-listing-grid-gap, var(--ds-spacing-4, 16px));
  --ds-detail-panel-item-gap: var(--ds-workspace-card-gap, var(--ds-spacing-3, 12px));
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--ds-surface-card);
  border-radius: var(--ds-workspace-card-radius, var(--ds-radius-lg));
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-color-bg-elevated) 88%, transparent),
    var(--ds-workspace-card-shadow, var(--ds-shadow-sm));
  animation: ds-detail-panel-arrive var(--ds-motion-calm, var(--ds-motion-normal))
    var(--ds-motion-ease-out, ease-out) both;
}

.ds-pattern-detail-panel.ds-engine-modern[data-part='root'][data-pattern='detail-panel'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-workspace-card-border, var(--ds-color-border));
}

/* ---- named container (W6-A): the panel root owns the width every descendant
