/* Disabled posture (K4-D Pass 2 adjudication): until now enabled and
   disabled buttons were indistinguishable. Canonical Button channels --
   cursor + opacity (the ghost surface stays transparent; the ink reads
   through the opacity, which is the ghost-disabled idiom). The native
   checkboxes get the cursor correction only: dimming rides the item row's
   own data-disabled posture (a global-disabled dim of the whole panel is a
   broader contract question, disclosed in the ficha). */
.rottay-transfer.rottay-transfer--modern [data-part='move-button']:disabled,
.rottay-transfer.rottay-transfer--modern [data-part='pagination-button']:disabled {
  cursor: var(--ds-transfer-button-disabled-cursor, var(--ds-button-disabled-cursor, not-allowed));
