 * (1) the search input's `onBlur` used to clear `borderColor` to the empty
 * string, which -- because React never re-renders on focus/blur -- left the
 * border on the browser's initial `currentColor` instead of restoring the
 * `--ds-transfer-search-input-border` token; deleting the imperative
 * handlers and shipping a rest border rule here restores the real default.
 * (2) the item-row hover's `#1677ff` hex fallback and the move-button
 * hover/press shadows were magic literals duplicated inline; they are
 * transcribed byte-exact below (still not tokenized -- filed as a proposal).
 *
 * INTERACTION MAPPING: the search focus ring, the item-row hover, and the
 * move-button hover/press all used to be imperative `.style.*` writes keyed
 * on native `:focus`/`:hover`/`:active` (and, for the move buttons, the
 * native `disabled` attribute the JS handlers also gated on --
 * `:not(:disabled)` reproduces `!disabled && count > 0` exactly). The item
