 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47).
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT: the outer `<div data-part='root'>` was Tailwind-only before
 * this migration (no component class at all). `rottay-colorpicker
 * rottay-colorpicker--modern` is added on it here, matching the class
 * family the sibling rustic engine already carries (`rottay-colorpicker
 * rottay-colorpicker--rustic`) and the `rottay-<comp> rottay-<comp>--modern`
 * idiom the modern Button/Input skins already use.
 *
 * PORTAL POSTURE: this engine's dropdown renders IN-TREE (a normal DOM
 * descendant of root, absolutely positioned by Tailwind utilities) --
 * unlike rustic, which portals to `document.body`. It stays root-scoped,
 * `.rottay-colorpicker.rottay-colorpicker--modern [data-part='dropdown']`.
 * Two divider `<div>`s (above the presets block, above the clear button)
 * carry no `data-part`; both are reached structurally via `:has()`, the
 * `input-number.css` idiom.
