}
/* Dropdown family (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint B). */
@layer rottay-engines {
/**
 * Modern AutoComplete skin (lane-A Quiet Premium pass over WO-SKIN-02
 * checkpoint B; Phase-B second pass 2026-07-31).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47):
 * every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity. Unlayered outranks
 * preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the wrapper `<div>`, which carries the pair
 * `ds-autocomplete ds-autocomplete--modern` + `data-part='root'` plus the
 * `data-size`/`data-status` state axes; every painted element is an IN-TREE
 * descendant with a `data-part` (AutoComplete never portals in either engine).
 * The `input` border reaches (0,4,0) via the two root classes (0,2,0) +
 * `[data-part='root']` + the descendant `[data-part]`.
 *
 * LANE-A PASS:
 * - The dropdown's position/z-index/padding/max-height and the clear button's
 *   positioning lived inline (the clear button rode the PHYSICAL `right-2`
 *   utility -- RTL broke it; now `inset-inline-end`). Both are skin-owned.
 * - The option rows' hover/active highlight used to ride the dead DaisyUI
 *   `active`/`disabled` class tokens (removed from the engine); the states
 *   are real rules below keyed on `data-active`/`data-disabled`, matching the
 *   Select/Cascader idiom, with the keyboard-focus ring and 44px coarse floor.
 * - The input gained hover/focus-visible states (its outline was suppressed
 *   with no replacement) and an inline-end reserve so the value never runs
 *   under the clear button.
 *
 * PHASE-B SECOND PASS:
 * - Per-size geometry drained from the engine's inline `getSizeStyle()` into
 *   `[data-size]` rules on the canonical `--ds-input-{sm,md,lg}-*` scale
 *   multiplied by `--ds-density-effective-scale` (Input/PasswordInput idiom):
 *   AutoComplete now tracks the tenant density plane like every sibling field.
 * - `status='error'|'warning'` (a contract prop the engine used to drop) is
 *   wired: the input reads the Input family's error/warning grammar --
 *   surface tint + border step + status-tinted focus ring, never a bare hue
 *   swap -- consuming the pre-existing `--ds-autocomplete-{error,warning}-border`
 *   tenant channels and the certified `--ds-input-*-bg/-shadow-focus` hooks.
 * - Option anatomy aligned with the Select dropdown grammar (the overlay this
 *   family shares its material contract with): transparent hairline frame at
 *   rest (no geometry jump on hover), hairline + primary-tinted wash + ink
 *   step on hover/`data-active`, density-scaled option floor, consuming the
 *   pre-existing `--ds-autocomplete-option-bg-hover` tenant channel.
 * - The empty posture adopts the Select empty well's spatial contract
 *   (dashed hairline, 4.5rem min-block, radius, muted helper ink) instead of
 *   a bare centered string; ink consumes the pre-existing
 *   `--ds-autocomplete-empty-color` channel.
 * - Placeholder/selection/autofill (webkit + standard) read the certified
 *   `--ds-input-*` channels; the input base surface reads the certified
 *   `--ds-input-bg` chain (never the generic `--ds-color-bg-input`, which
 *   resolves near-black under the TMM DB projection -- the OTP CONTROL
 *   SURFACE law), with `--ds-autocomplete-bg` kept as the tenant override.
 * - Clear-button hover no longer flashes the ERROR hue (a destructive miscue
 *   for a neutral reset): it reads the Input clear grammar's ink step.
 * - `popupMatchSelectWidth={false}` (contract) resolves to content width
 *   bounded by a proto max (Select's 28rem dropdown dial), still viewport-safe.
 *
 * PHASE B2 (P2 deep pass, 2026-07-31):
 * - The input gained an accessible name (axe `label` critical; Mentions
 *   K4-D idiom): placeholder is the floor, `autocomplete.input_label` the
 *   localized default (engine).
 * - Option rows grew the governed `option-label` slot (Cascader/Mentions
 *   parity): the ellipsis lives on the flex child, never on the row.
 * - The empty row inside the listbox carries role="option" + aria-disabled
 *   (aria-required-children; Mentions idiom).
 * - Hover states paint their touch `:active` equivalents (input border,
 *   option wash, clear-button ink step -- 4th-tanda law).
 */

@keyframes ds-autocomplete-slide-in {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-4px) scale(0.98);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
  }
}

.ds-autocomplete.ds-autocomplete--modern[data-part='root'] {
  position: relative;
}

.ds-autocomplete.ds-autocomplete--modern[data-part='root'] [data-part='input-wrapper'] {
  position: relative;
}

.ds-autocomplete.ds-autocomplete--modern[data-part='root'] [data-part='input'] {
  inline-size: 100%;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-border);
  border-radius: var(--ds-radius-md);
  /* Certified Input control surface chain (OTP CONTROL SURFACE law): the
     generic --ds-color-bg-input resolves near-black under TMM DB; the tenant
     override --ds-autocomplete-bg stays first. */
  background: var(--ds-autocomplete-bg, var(--ds-input-bg, var(--ds-surface-control)));
  color: var(--ds-color-text-primary);
  caret-color: var(--ds-input-caret-color, var(--ds-input-border-focus, var(--ds-color-primary)));
  outline: none;
  transition:
