 *
 *   .rottay-toast-container > *  (0,1,0)  -> animation: ds-toast-enter 300ms ...
 *
 * That selector matches exactly the stack-item wrappers styled below. It declares
 * ONLY `animation`; the wrapper never carried an inline `animation` and this file
 * declares none, so the rule is LIVE today and stays LIVE -- there was never any
 * suppression to preserve on that channel.
 *
 * The rule does interact with the `transform` below, and the interaction is
 * unchanged by the migration: a running animation overrides the element's
 * `transform` property regardless of origin or layer, so `ds-toast-enter` drives
 * the transform for its 300ms; with no `forwards` fill it then hands back to the
 * winning normal declaration -- previously the inline transform, now this rule.
 * Same value, same handoff. The `.rottay-toast-container` class name is therefore
 * load-bearing and must not be renamed.
