}
@layer rottay-engines {
/**
 * Rustic Tour skin (WO-SKIN-04 checkpoint P).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47).
 *
 * PORTAL: both engines portal via a DIRECT `createPortal(…, document.body)` — not through
 * the shared `Portal` util. Every rule is standalone on the root class.
 *
 * THE MASK COLOUR IS RUNTIME AND STAYS JS-DRIVEN, via the `--ds-tour-mask-color` custom
 * property stamped on the root (see the modern skin's header for the full rationale). The
 * var is referenced with NO fallback on purpose: a `mask` object with no `color` leaves it
 * unset, which drops both dependent declarations — exactly reproducing today's
 * `backgroundColor: undefined` and invalid `0 0 0 9999px undefined`.
 *
 * This engine's default mask colour is the literal `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)`; modern's is
 * `--ds-color-alpha-black-50`. Both are resolved in JS and preserved.
 *
 * TOKENS: this engine references a dedicated 12-name `--ds-tour-*` family. NONE of those
 * names is defined anywhere in the tokens tree, so the hex fallbacks below are what every
 * tenant actually sees today. They are transcribed verbatim; defining the family is a
 * visual change and belongs in its own work order.
 *
 * The surface's border was three LONGHANDS (`borderWidth` / `borderStyle` / `borderColor`).
 * It is re-formed here as an atomic SHORTHAND per `data-type` — `0 solid transparent` for
 * the non-primary case, which is exactly what the longhand trio computed to.
 *
 * NEITHER engine has any hover/focus/active feedback anywhere. That absence is the shipped
 * behaviour and is preserved; do not add interaction paint.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): every colored border repeats its `data-part` to clear the tenant `*`
 * border-color floor at (0,3,1). `transparent` still paints (it wins the tenant colour), so
 * the non-primary branch is held to the floor too.
