@layer rottay-components {
/**
 * MobileHeader skin (WO-SKIN-04 checkpoint N).
 *
 * ENGINE-AGNOSTIC: MobileHeader has no `engines/` split — it composes Box/Flex/
 * Text, which resolve through the engine system themselves. One skin file, no
 * engine modifier class.
 *
 * LAYER: imported by `facade/entrypoints/base.css` and
 * `facade/entrypoints/styles.css` into `layer(rottay-components)` (the old
 * "unlayered" note predates the wiring).
 *
 * ELEMENT-LEVEL CLASSES, NOT BARE `data-part` DESCENDANTS: `data-part='trigger'`
 * and `data-part='label'` are shared vocabulary across a dozen components
 * (Dropdown, Popconfirm, ContextMenu, Menu, FloatButton, …). MobileHeader's
 * `leftAction` / `rightAction` / `children` slots accept arbitrary consumer
 * nodes, so a descendant `[data-part='trigger']` rule would repaint any DS
 * component the caller drops into a slot. Each painted element therefore carries
 * its own class and is matched by a COMPOUND selector.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * border-color floor at (0,3,1). The root's `border-bottom` carries a real
 * color, so it must reach (0,4,0); with only ONE root class that is bought by
 * `data-sticky`, which the engine always stamps ('true'|'false') — repeating
 * an attribute is forbidden. The back button's `border: none` is a color-free
 * reset, exempt from the floor.
