@layer rottay-engines {
/**
 * Modern Divider skin (WO-SKIN-05 checkpoint L).
 *
 * Imported into `rottay-engines`, above the Modern framework's bounded
 * `rottay-framework` layer. The engine emits no generic DaisyUI `.divider`
 * classname: protected DS anatomy owns both line segments, preventing
 * duplicate framework pseudo-elements and keeping RTL logical positioning in
 * the component contract rather than the application.
 *
 * `color`/`thickness` are caller-overridable free-form props (`DividerProps`
 * accepts any CSS color string and either a preset or a raw px number), so
 * the resolved line value cannot be enumerated into a finite `data-*`
 * lookup the way a closed-enum channel can. It rides the `--ds-divider-line`
 * custom-property hatch instead -- set inline, every render, to the exact
 * string the removed `borderTop`/`borderLeft` keys used to hold (the same
 * hatch the migration kit sanctions for a runtime-computed value); the
 * fallback below matches `DEFAULT_COLORS.modern` + `THICKNESS_MAP.thin` +
 * the default `solid` variant so it is never actually reached in practice.
 * Label styling is keyed by the protected `data-plain` anatomy signal, so
 * typography and color remain tenant-remappable CSS rather than inline paint.
 *
 * Layer ownership, not specificity escalation, makes this first-party paint
 * authoritative while inline caller geometry remains the final local seam.
 */

/* ---- line: with-text spans (horizontal only -- `hasChildren` in the engine
        requires the horizontal orientation, so a vertical divider never
        renders these parts; the vertical line lives on the root rule below). ---- */
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part="root"][data-orientation="horizontal"]
