 * `stat-value` classes, so this skin is the single paint owner of the
 * title/value typography through the `data-part` hooks. The `[data-tenant]
 * .stat-title` / `.stat-value` rules in `engines/modern/theme.css` are now
 * DEAD for this engine and are listed for the coordinator's theme.css
 * cleanup (they were layered and lost to this unlayered file anyway).
 * The title/value geometry (line-height, margins, affix gaps) moved here
 * from the engine's inline styles; affix gaps are logical properties.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): every value here is non-border paint except the skeleton's
 * `border-radius`, which carries no color -- so (0,3,0) clears preflight and the
 * (0,4,0) border floor does not apply. Child combinators keep the rules off any
 * `data-part` a caller's `prefix`/`suffix`/`title` node may itself carry. Values
 * transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`.
 *
 * PHASE B (second premium pass): the hover lift is gated under
 * `@media (hover: hover)` (hover law; a passive metric has no touch press
 * semantics, so no :active twin); the trend icon rule paints the governed
 * non-color half of `valueType` (icon shape + hidden localized text in the
 * engine; hue was the only signal before); and the affix chip floor rides
 * the tenant density plane via the `--ds-density-effective-scale` idiom.
 */

.rottay-statistic.rottay-statistic--modern[data-part='root'] {
  min-width: 0;
  color: var(--ds-statistic-color, var(--ds-color-text-primary));
  transition:
    transform var(--ds-motion-fast) var(--ds-motion-ease-out),
    filter var(--ds-motion-fast) var(--ds-motion-ease-out);
}

/* Pointer-fine hover only (hover law): a passive metric has no touch press
   semantics, so no :active twin — touch simply skips the lift. */
@media (hover: hover) {
  .rottay-statistic.rottay-statistic--modern[data-part='root'][data-loading='false']:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    filter: saturate(1.025);
  }
}

.rottay-statistic.rottay-statistic--modern[data-part='root'] > [data-part='title'] {
  /* CONTRAST LAW (K3-A Pass 2, axe color-contrast/serious on BOTH sources):
     the DS-default title channel #737373 fails AA on the tinted page
     surfaces (4.44:1 on bithire #F4F8FB, 4.40:1 on TMM #FBF6EC). The ink
     deepens 30% toward the source's own primary text ink -- hue-faithful
     (measured worst source: TMM 70% = 5.49:1). A tenant's explicit
     `--ds-statistic-title-ink` stays raw. */
  color: var(
    --ds-statistic-title-ink,
    color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--ds-statistic-title-color, var(--ds-color-text-secondary)) 70%,
      var(--ds-color-text-primary) 30%
