/* ---- state law (B1.4/B1.5): semantic tones never ride hue alone. Success,
        warning, error and their legacy aliases (red/green/blue) get a surface
        keyline THROUGH the fill, so a state node reads as a ringed disc
        against the flat neutral (primary/gray) journey nodes -- shape is the
        second channel, hue the first. The keyline follows the marker's
        border-radius; forced colors strips it and re-maps the fill below. ---- */
