 * unnamed `base` layer, so a layered rule loses to preflight regardless of
 * specificity. That matters more here than anywhere else in this checkpoint: the
 * input chrome is written as LONGHANDS (`border-width`/`border-style`/
 * `border-color`), and preflight kills `border-width` on every element. Unlayered
 * is the only reason the 1px input border survives at all (P-76).
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the `<form>` carrying `ds-pattern-form-builder ds-engine-rustic`
 * + `data-part='root'`. This engine has no loading branch (it destructures
 * `loading` and never reads it -- a real, pre-existing cross-engine gap the
 * contract test asserts explicitly rather than papering over).
