 * HATCH (contract §5.1, kit "runtime-computed"): `getVariantTone(colorVariant)` /
 * `getVariantTone(status.color)` are prop-selected, and the pre-step stamped NO
 * variant/status attribute on `icon-badge`/`status-pill` to key a CSS rule on.
 * Their computed tone rides a `--ds-*` custom property set inline (uncounted) and
 * is consumed here. `icon-badge` sets `color` on itself so the composed glyph
 * inherits `currentColor`; `status-pill` sets a `--…-fg` the composed `status-pill-text`
 * consumes at (0,5,0), because a `Text` will not inherit `color` past the
 * typography skin.
 *
 * GLASS LAW: the context card's `backdrop-filter: blur(8px)` was default-ON
 * glass — it now rides `--ds-edit-header-context-card-filter` with a `none`
 * default; a tenant opts the blur back in through the channel.
 *
 * MOTION: the enter animation rides the real `--ds-motion-slow` rung (the old
 * `--ds-motion-calm` is a tenant-artifact ghost outside foundation).
 *
 * BREADCRUMB: own grammar (the §4 anatomy tests pin
 * `breadcrumb-link/separator/item`); composing the Breadcrumb primitive is a
 * contract-level migration, documented in the engine header.
 */

/* ─── SHARED EDIT+FORM: hero-panel archetype gradient (buildPatternStyle) ─── */

