 * sub-components (PresenceBar, PresenceTypingIndicator, LiveCursor), each its
 * own scope island carrying `ds-presence-<export>` on its own root plus
 * `data-part` on every painted descendant.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before
 * Tailwind's base layer, so a layered rule loses to preflight regardless of
 * specificity. Unlayered outranks preflight and still yields to a caller's
 * inline `style`.
 *
 * RUNTIME STAYS INLINE under exact executable floors: PresenceBar's avatar ring
 * `border` and avatar-initials `color` (both `ringColor = user.color ||
 * DEFAULT_COLOR`), and LiveCursor's `cursor-badge` `background` (same shape
 * via `cursorColor`) are genuine per-user caller data and are not represented
 * here at all -- they remain exactly as written in index.tsx. LiveCursor's
 * SVG `fill={cursorColor}` (per-user, a JSX presentation attribute, not a
 * style key) remains runtime-authored. The outline stroke is static and is
 * owned by the scoped skin rule below. The three inline identity sites carry
 * `floor: 3`; the intrinsic SVG fill carries an independent
 * `runtimeSvgFloor: 1`.
 *
 * RUNTIME HATCH: `--ds-presence-badge-ring` carries the overflow badge's ring
 * WIDTH, which tracks the `size` prop (`sm`: 2px, `md`: 2.5px) and has no
 * stamped attribute to key CSS off of; the width is set inline (uncounted
 * quoted custom-property key) and consumed here alongside the static
 * style/color that make up the rest of the border-color site.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48), single scope class per export (0,1,0):
 *   - NON-BORDER paint on a Box (background, border-radius) reaches (0,3,0)
 *     with the class + the descendant `data-part` repeated once (class(1) +
 *     part(2) = 3). The avatar's `<img>` fallback has no `data-part` of its
 *     own (a single, unconditional child needs none); its border-radius rule
 *     buys the same three units from the class + the parent `[data-part=
 *     'avatar']` repeated, plus the `img` element selector (which adds to the
 *     c-column only, not required for the floor but free).
 *   - `color` on a composed `Text` (`overflow-badge-count`, `label`) must
 *     EXCEED the Typography engine skins' own `[data-color='default']` rule,
 *     which both modern and rustic ship at (0,4,0). Both Texts here render
 *     with an unset `color` prop, so they always carry `data-color='default'`
 *     and always compete. Reaching (0,5,0) needs class + part repeated to
 *     four (class(1) + part(4) = 5).
 *   - A BORDER COLOR must reach (0,4,0): class + part repeated to three
 *     (class(1) + part(3) = 4). The overflow badge's ring is the one
