 * HIGHLIGHT LAW: the recommended plan reads as frame + badge (shape + text),
 * never a vertical accent rail and never a glow — a 2px primary frame with a
 * quiet tint. In forced colors the frame re-expresses as Highlight and the
 * feature states read by icon shape (check vs cross), never by hue.
 *
 * RESPONSIVE: this is a comparison TABLE — its value is cross-plan row
 * alignment, so narrow containers keep the grid and scroll horizontally with
 * a sticky feature column instead of re-stacking into per-plan cards (which
 * would either break row alignment or duplicate the DOM for assistive tech).
