 * the three engines render one shared foundation engine today. This file is the
 * modern-only remediation layer and loads in layer rottay-engines, which sorts
 * AFTER rottay-components, so these rules win without `!important` and without
 * touching classic/rustic paint. Engine-specific rules scope on
 * `.ds-engine-modern`, which only the modern engine wrapper stamps on the root.
 */

/* ---- empty-state frame: the composed Empty primitive (P09) paints itself;
        the pattern only grants it the full twelve-track row. Unscoped on
        purpose: the part is shared anatomy (the foundation engine renders it
        for every engine), only its paint is primitive-owned. ---- */
.ds-pattern-record-facts .ds-record-facts__empty {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  min-width: 0;
}

/* ---- long values wrap word-first (the shared skin's `anywhere` breaks
        mid-word even when a word boundary fits) and numerals stay tabular so
        dense metric values align column-to-column (CRA-01 law; the value is a
        consumer ReactNode, so the `ds-nums-tabular` utility cannot reach it
        and the channel lives here) ---- */
.ds-pattern-record-facts.ds-engine-modern .ds-record-facts__value,
.ds-pattern-record-facts.ds-engine-modern .ds-record-facts__supporting {
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
